{"duration_api_ms":125002,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"464bda29-4a81-4d24-9954-db1223732230","total_cost_usd":0.6659272,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39921,"cache_read_input_tokens":433376,"output_tokens":12989,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5665},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39921,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1184,"cache_read_input_tokens":50634,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1513,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1513},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":26,"outputTokens":12989,"cacheReadInputTokens":433376,"cacheCreationInputTokens":39921,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6659272,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":5665,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":39921,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":13,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I fixed the three decoder defects in `src/urllib3/response.py`, using only the standard library. The release gate still fails: 3 of the 4 checks pass, and the fourth fails because optional third-party packages aren't installed. So this is **not release-ready** as the gate is defined.\n\n## Final `run_checks.py` result (`Ran 4 tests`, `FAILED (failures=1)`)\n\n| Check | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_gzip_multi_member_bounded_read` | FAIL | **ok** |\n| `test_raw_deflate_eof_flush_streaming` | FAIL | **ok** |\n| `test_reject_decode_toggle_before_consuming` | FAIL | **ok** |\n| `test_optional_brotli_and_zstd_codecs_available` | FAIL | **FAIL**: \"BLOCKER: optional third-party 'brotli'/'brotlicffi' package is not installed in this environment\" |\n\nThe last check only tests whether `brotli`/`brotlicffi` and `zstandard` (or Python 3.14's `compression.zstd`) are installed. Code changes can't make it pass under the standard-library-only rule. It will pass only once those packages are installed or the gate's requirement changes, and that's your call.\n\n## What I changed\n1. **Multi-member gzip:** when a bounded read ended exactly where one gzip member ends, the leftover bytes were fed back into the finished decompressor, which repeated the next member's data. The decoder now starts a new decompressor for the next member before stopping at the length limit.\n2. **Missing data at the end of the stream:**\n   - At end of stream, `read()` returned `b\"\"` without flushing the decoder, so the last bytes of raw deflate output were lost. It now flushes first and buffers what comes out.\n   - The bounded-read loop now flushes as soon as the raw stream is empty.\n   - For chained encodings like `deflate, gzip`, the flush used to cover only one decoder. Now each decoder's leftover output is passed down the chain and flushed too.\n   - A repeated `read(cache_content=True)` at end of stream no longer overwrites the cached `_body` with `b\"\"`.\n3. **Switching to `decode_content=False`:** `read()` now raises `RuntimeError` before touching `fp` or the buffered decoded data. `read(0, decode_content=False)` still returns `b\"\"`. Since `stream()` goes through `read()`, it gets the same behaviour.\n\n## Extra checks beyond the gate\n- **Round-trip sweep:** I tested `read`, `read1`, `stream` and \"read 5 bytes, then read the rest\" with gzip (several members), raw deflate, zlib deflate, `deflate, gzip` and `gzip, deflate`. Payloads were 0 to 6000 bytes, read in sizes of 1, 7, 64, 1024 and 1025 bytes and unbounded. Every case returned exactly the original data.\n- **Caching and the decode switch:** cached bodies survive repeated reads, and switching to `decode_content=False` leaves `fp` and the buffer untouched. Responses with no content-encoding, or read raw throughout, behave as before.\n\n**One issue I left alone:** `stream(amt=None)` loops forever when the response wraps a plain `BytesIO`. `_raw_read` closes the underlying file only on bounded reads, and none of my edits touch that path. A real `http.client` response closes itself at end of stream, so this probably only affects test setups, but it's worth knowing about.","ttft_ms":2151,"type":"result","duration_ms":377049,"uuid":"5383dff9-8021-41de-8ab4-1f4ac77a90c5","ttft_stream_ms":1491,"time_to_request_ms":232,"first_content_frame_ms":1491,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-23T22:59:00.503Z"}

